    "definitions": {
      "short": "a pace or regular step",
      "usage": "pace, step.",
      "full": "H6806. tsaad [ צַ֫עַד ] noun masculine 2Sam 6:13 step, pace ; — absolute צָ֑עַד Prov 30:29 ; suffix צַעֲדוֺ Jer 10:3 ; Prov 6:9 , etc.; plural construct צַעֲדֵי Job 18:7 ; suffix צְעָדַי 31:4 , etc.; &#8212; 1 literally step, pace , 2Sam 6:13 , תַּחְתֵּנִי צַעֲדִי תַּרְחִיב 22:37 = Psa 18:37 , i.e. givest me firm footing, צ ׳מֵטִיבֵי Prov 30:29 = making a good step , stately in march; Lam 4:18 (|| לָ֑כֶת ). 2 step, steps , in figure of course of life, fortune: singular צ יֵצַר ׳לֹא Prov 4:12 ; || דֶּרֶךְ Jer 10:23 ; Prov 16:9 ; Job 14:16 ; 31:4 ; 34:21 , אוֺנוֺ צַעֲדֵי 18:7 (compare Prov 4:12 above); אַגִּידֶנּוּ מִסְמַּרעָֿדַי Proverbs 31:37; of harlot 5:5 figurative, יִתְמֹ֑כוּ צְעָדֶיהָ שְׁאוֺל .",
